// S~S  SimpleSal signal starts  S~S

// [Event Databases.note]               search in ssTEA source files for a reference to this file.
//
   -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Central concept for ssTEA: where are the allocations made of the data structures used with ssTEA?
   There is within ssE event data management a basic "event database" where events are described;
   allocation of the Event's AboutEvent data is controlled by independent factors: location and access.
   The Event data structure is the primary requirement per active event, as accessible memory.
   -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   The solution should be the same for a User with one, 5 and 50 events.  The location only matters
   when the User wants to replace the simple mechanism built into SSE for DB data structure allocs.
   The location choice is based on memory constraints or attributes of memory holding critical info.
   -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Choose one location for Event data structures to be allocated, according to "oneof_allocates".
   -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   The "trusted" choice is based on whether ssE can let the App have access to ssE data in ssE_AboutEv.
   Opt In to limit the allocation of ssE_AboutEv to a single copy, accessible by the App and by ssE.
   Opt Out to create a duplicate App ssE_AboutEv copy for each ssE_AboutEv in ssE; kept up to date by ssE.
   -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//
   -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   EvInfo data is the ssTEA knowledge about all events.  ssE_AboutEv is the API Agency data (type
   and variable) describing one instance of an event, as specified by the User of the Agency Api.
   There is one EvInfo for each Event actively managed by ssTEA; data is privately kept by ssTEA.
   In each EvInfo is a pointer to the About Event (ssE_pAboutEv) used by ssTEA to manage the Event.
   About Event data pointed to is either a copy of ssTEA's (App not trusted) or ssTEA's (trusted).
   -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//
   -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   the declaration of the AboutEv Database interface is made by ssTEA; it may be implemented by App.
   Of App or ssE, implementation includes the database allocation and a set of Get/Put operations.
   -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   NOT declared by the App, use ssE's               void    AboutEvDB_dbOp_Init_DB (void);
   IMPLEMENTED by the App only if configured        void    AboutEvDB_dbOp_Init_DB (void) { ..... }

    #ifdef SSE_ONEOF_ABOUTEVDB_ALLOC_BY_APP            in App source file
    #ifdef SSE_ONEOF_ABOUTEVDB_ALLOC_BY_SSE            in ssTEA source file
//
    ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Software that manages conditions over time and takes action based on conditions needs data.
    Software that instantiates and operates an FSM needs to maintain data about the FSM itself.

    The "About Event" structure describes an Event with just enough information to grant Agency.
    Depending on the degree of trust in the skills of the App software developer, two choices are
    available for the data structures central to ssTEA algorithms: trust, or don't trust, the App.
    An App that is not trusted has the same information about Events, but only a copy of ssTEA's.
    ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    The App, in the form of ssUI, instantiates API data structures for each Event: an "Event API".
    Each of the App's Event API structures points to About Event information for that Event.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    The ssE Event Info database is used by ssA algorithms implementing the Agency Root FSM of ssTEA.
    This explains the allocation count, based on the number of events, and not the idea of trust.

    The database is only referenced by ssA for Active Events, where the Api FSM state is not Off.
    The transition to Api FSM state On consumes an EvInfo and an About Event for the Event Info.
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    ssE_EvInfo_t  ssE_EvInfos[SSE_EVINFO_ALLOC_CT];
//

// S~S  SimpleSal signal ends  S~S
